  THE FEEDBACK LINE RE-OPENS, WITH A NAMED REQUIREMENT. A perfect
  controller holds F1 to 6.0 Hz at zero delay and still removes half
  the open-loop error at v62's 165 ms round trip and at the shipped 905 ms. aimhold measured ONE
  gain, derived by matching the correction to the error, which sets loop
  gain near 1 where residual error is ~1/2 -- and a proportional
  controller needs L >> 1. The learned-controller question is live again.
